IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Frustrated Contracts Act 1959 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation -- LAYER 1, THE NOUNS.
--
-- Nouns only: the facts a witness of ordinary competence could state about one frustrated contract, and the few
-- choices the Act names.  There is no rule here; every rule is in a module that imports this one.
-- The unit of a case is ONE CONTRACT (and, within it, one sum, one benefit or one provision).
--
-- Where the Act leaves a judgment to the court ("if it considers it just", "as appears to the court"), the judgment is
-- a field the person or the court supplies, never a computation (a MAYBE BOOLEAN where the court may not yet have
-- decided: NOTHING then means "not yet decided").
-- Where the Act borrows a term it does not define ("frustrated", "charterparty", "contract of insurance", "specific goods",
-- "perished") or another Act's rule (section 7 of the Sale of Goods Act 1979), the fact is asked as a plain yes/no.

§ `Nouns -- one contract`

-- s 2(1) and s 3: the facts about the contract as a whole.
@ref s 2(1), s 3(1), s 3(2), s 3(5)
DECLARE `Contract facts` HAS
    `the contract has become impossible of performance or been otherwise frustrated` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the parties to the contract have for that reason been discharged from the further performance of the contract` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the date the parties were so discharged` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the date the contract was made` IS A DATE
    `the Government is a party to the contract` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the contract is a charterparty` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the charterparty is a time charterparty` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the charterparty is a charterparty by way of demise` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the contract is a contract for the carriage of goods by sea` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the contract is a contract of insurance` IS A BOOLEAN
    `section 7 of the Sale of Goods Act 1979 applies to the contract` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the contract is for the sale, or for the sale and delivery, of specific goods` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the contract is frustrated by reason of the fact that the goods have perished` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 3(3): a provision of the contract itself.
@ref s 3(3)
DECLARE `Contract provision facts` HAS
    `the contract contains a provision which, upon its true construction, is intended to have effect in the event of circumstances arising which operate, or would but for that provision operate, to frustrate the contract` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the contract contains a provision which, upon its true construction, is intended to have effect whether such circumstances arise or not` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 3(4): a part of the contract.
@ref s 3(4)
DECLARE `Severable part facts` HAS
    `it appears to the court that a part of the contract can properly be severed from the remainder of the contract` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `the part was wholly performed before the time of discharge` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the part was so performed except for the payment in respect of that part of sums which are or can be ascertained under the contract` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 3(4): which portion of a severable contract a question is asked about.
@ref s 3(4)
DECLARE `Portion of a contract` IS ONE OF
    `the severed part`
    `the remainder of the contract`

§ `Nouns -- money`

-- s 2(2): one sum paid, or payable, to a party in pursuance of the contract.
@ref s 2(2)
DECLARE `Sum facts` HAS
    `the amount of the sum` IS A NUMBER
    `the sum was paid` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the sum was paid or payable to a party in pursuance of the contract` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the sum was paid or fell payable before the time when the parties were so discharged` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 2(3), s 2(4)(a), s 2(5): the expenses a party incurred, and what the court includes when estimating them.
-- The two "sum the court includes" fields are 0 where the court includes nothing under s 2(5).
@ref s 2(3), s 2(4)(a), s 2(5)
DECLARE `Expenses facts` HAS
    `expenses were incurred before the time of discharge in, or for the purpose of, the performance of the contract` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the amount of those expenses` IS A NUMBER
    `the sum the court includes in respect of overhead expenses` IS A NUMBER
    `the sum the court includes in respect of work or services performed personally by that party` IS A NUMBER

§ `Nouns -- benefits`

-- s 2(4): one valuable benefit that a party obtained.
@ref s 2(4), s 2(4)(a)
DECLARE `Benefit facts` HAS
    `a party to the contract has obtained a valuable benefit by reason of anything done by any other party to the contract in, or for the purpose of, the performance of the contract` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the benefit was obtained before the time of discharge` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the benefit is a payment of money to which section 2(2) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the value of the benefit to the party obtaining it` IS A NUMBER
    `the sums paid or payable by the benefited party to any other party in pursuance of the contract and retained or recoverable by that party under section 2(3)` IS A NUMBER

-- s 2(4): the matters the court has regard to ("all the circumstances of the case and, in particular -- (a) ... (b) ...").
@ref s 2(4), s 2(4)(a), s 2(4)(b)
DECLARE `Matter for section 2(4)` IS ONE OF
    `the expenses incurred before the time of discharge by the benefited party (paragraph (a))`
    `the effect, in relation to that benefit, of the circumstances giving rise to the frustration of the contract (paragraph (b))`
    `some other circumstance of the case`
    `something that is not a circumstance of the case`

-- s 2(7): a person who assumed obligations in consideration of a benefit conferred on someone else.
@ref s 2(7)
DECLARE `Obligor facts` HAS
    `a person has assumed obligations under the contract` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the obligations were assumed in consideration of the conferring of a benefit by another party to the contract upon another person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person on whom the benefit was conferred is a party to the contract` IS A BOOLEAN

§ `Nouns -- insurance`

-- s 2(6): insurance sums that have become payable to a party.
@ref s 2(6)
DECLARE `Insurance facts` HAS
    `the court is considering whether any sum ought to be recovered or retained under section 2 by the party` IS A BOOLEAN
    `sums have, by reason of the circumstances giving rise to the frustration of the contract, become payable to the party under a contract of insurance` IS A BOOLEAN
    `there was an obligation to insure imposed by an express term of the frustrated contract` IS A BOOLEAN
    `there was an obligation to insure imposed by or under an enactment` IS A BOOLEAN
